<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport"
        content="width=device-width, user-scalable=no, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, minimum-scale=1.0">
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="ie=edge">
  <title>Document</title>
</head>
<body>
Hello {{recipient}},
<br><br>
Dispute #{{disputeId}} of swap <a
  href="https://app.fiatx.co/swap/{{orderId}}">#{{orderId}}</a> has passed the
vote reveal phase.
This means mediators can no longer reveal their vote. It is now time for
the <b>appeal phase</b>. <br><br> In this phase, swap participants
(liquidity provider or taker) can appeal the ruling of the dispute before
execution by miners.
<br><br>
Ruling: <b style="font-size:22px; color: orange;">{{outcome}}</b> <br>
Appeal Phase Ends In: <b style="font-size:
22px; color: darkolivegreen;">{{appealPhaseHoursLeft}}</b>
<br><br>
{{#if participant}}
  <h3 style="color: indianred">WARNING</h3>
  <ul style="color: indianred">
    <li>Appeal requires a bond that is doubled for every new appeal.
      It is calculated as <i>baseCost x numberOfAppeals</i> where
      <i>baseCost</i> =
      <i>{{cost}}</i> P2P.
    </li>
    <li>Just like the appeal bond, mediators are doubled for every new appeal.
    </li>
    <li>You will not be able to appeal the ruling after the appeal phased
      elapses.
    </li>
  </ul>
{{/if}}
<br>
<ul>
  <li><a href="https://app.fiatx.co/swap/{{orderId}}">View Swap Order</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://app.fiatx.co/swap/{{orderId}}">How Disputes Work</a></li>
</ul>
<br>
{{app}}
</body>
</html>
